margate was among 101 towns from across  england selected a bid for funding from  the government's towns fund initiative  this is a once-in-a-generation  opportunity to invest in local projects  drive growth and improve the environment  for the benefit of the whole community  the town deal comes at an important and  exciting time in margate's history the  town has faced its challenges over the  last 50 years and now is the time to  come together to make sure it has a  thriving economy 365 days a year  at the heart of the town deal is the  town investment plan which sets out a  long-term vision and strategy for  margate the investment plan makes the  case for a 29 million pound investment  supporting projects themed around four  interlinking interventions these build  on what makes margate so special and  deliver change that will benefit local  people and visitors for years to come  margate's growing creative and cultural  economy is an opportunity not to be  missed the first intervention is  therefore a nine million pound  investment in scaling margate's creative  production and skills it will establish  a creative land trust to support  projects stretching from the high street  to the theatre royal building spaces for  creative production and education  potential locations include the former  marks and spencers primark and other key  sites within the high street investment  will bring life back to the town centre  linking the coast to the historic hawley  square and establishing a creative  economic hub driving jobs skills  education and engagement  in its heyday margate was known as a  place for well-being and tourism the  second intervention is a 6.5 million  pound investment in coastal well-being  to support projects across margate's  coastline creating new and surprising  experiences for visitors establishing  better links between the town centre  north down road and the coastline will  deliver an improved network of  connections and encourage people to  explore beyond the seafront  the third intervention focuses on public  realm and connections with a 4.5 million  pound targeted investment in the town  centre coastline and residential areas  making it easier to get around and  improving visitor amenities this will  better connect north down road to the  town centre and create attractive public  spaces as well as enhancing cycling and  walking infrastructure  margate's past has a role to play in its  future the fourth intervention is  therefore a nine million pound  investment in well-loved heritage assets  and will help secure a sustainable  future for the dreamland cinema complex  and the winter gardens which benefits  the wider town  it will create new enterprise and  cultural spaces for both visitors and  the community it will also support the  development of feasibility plans for the  future of important landmarks including  the arlington arcade the old town hall  and the lido  the town investment plan has now been  submitted to the ministry of housing  communities and local government thank  you to everyone who took the time to get  involved and share their views we're  currently waiting to hear back from the  government and in the meantime the town  deal board and project team continue to  work in partnership with stakeholders  local businesses and the community  you can read the tan investment plan in  full keep up to date with how the deal  progresses and sign up to receive news  at margate  dot  towndeal.co.uk
 

